WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.000
You

00:30.000 --> 00:32.000
You

00:32.000 --> 00:49.600
You fellow delegates the president of the United States of America

01:02.000 --> 01:14.000
The charter of the United Nations, which you are now signing, is a solid structure upon which we can build for a better world.

01:14.000 --> 01:18.000
History will honor you for it.

01:18.000 --> 01:27.000
Between the victory in Europe and the final victory in Japan, in this most destructive of all wars,

01:27.000 --> 01:32.000
you have won a victory against war itself.

01:32.000 --> 01:42.000
If we had had this charter a few years ago, and above all the will to use it, millions now dead would be alive.

01:42.000 --> 01:51.000
If we should falter in the future in our will to use it, millions now living will surely die.

01:51.000 --> 02:01.000
What you have accomplished in San Francisco shows how well these lessons of military and economic cooperation have been learned.

02:01.000 --> 02:10.000
You have created a great instrument for peace and security and human progress in the world.

02:10.000 --> 02:13.000
The world must now use it.

02:13.000 --> 02:24.000
With this charter, the world can begin to look forward to the time when all worthy human beings may be permitted to live decently as free people.

02:24.000 --> 02:30.000
This new structure of peace is rising upon strong foundations.

02:30.000 --> 02:45.000
Let us not fail to grasp this supreme chance to establish a worldwide rule of reason, to create an enduring peace under the guidance of God.

02:45.000 --> 03:00.000
Thank you very much.

03:15.000 --> 03:28.000
Thank you.

